  "telemetry-default": {
    "value": "on-by-default",
    "claimId": "zozo:OWN-03",
    "evidenceIds": [
      "zozo:privacy",
      "zozo:review-telemetry-runtime"
    ],
    "checkedAt": "2026-11-26",
    "rationale": "Scoped to the vendor-hosted Stack. With hosted control-plane bootstrap (ZOZO_CONTROL_PLANE_URL and token), the public npm 0.41.9 dispatch supervisor starts timers that POST status/health, admission, active and pending run counts and aggregate usage to the Zozo control plane (/v1/status, /v1/usage); the data-and-privacy guide says the control plane receives defined health and aggregate usage fields. These are vendor diagnostics sent without a user opt-in. The accountless local Stack without that bootstrap sends none of this and has no analytics or crash client. Model-provider requests and local journal logs are not telemetry.",
    "researcher": "agent:ADE-209",
    "contentHash": "74a98d67576b0afa58f089292ea448c6434c9f87147cd08fac20b38a4d97e8d3",
    "review": {
